@startuml recovery-flow
' ============================================================================
' Crash-recovery flow — open → load checkpoint image → scan the durable WAL
' tail from checkpoint_lsn → reconcile per term by max commit-generation →
' rebuild the overlay → resume serving. The acked-vs-unacked fork is explicit.
' Source of truth:
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/recovery.rs  (redo-only ARIES recovery,
'                                            reconcile_lww, generation_of)
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/wal/header.rs (checkpoint_lsn, rank_regime, magic)
'   src/persistent_artrie/{mmap_ctor,io_uring_ctor}.rs  (open path)
' ARIES — Mohan et al. 1992, doi:10.1145/128765.128770 (redo-only here).
' Color key:  blue  #BBDEFB = durable on-disk read (header / image / WAL tail)
'             amber #FFE0B2 = control / reconcile decision (frontier)
'             green #C8E6C9 = in-memory rebuild / serving
'             red   #FFCDD2 = a write that was NEVER durable (dropped)
'             grey  #ECEFF1 = terminal
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam wrapWidth 230
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
  DiamondBorderColor #F9A825
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFE0B2
}

title Crash recovery — redo-only WAL replay from the last checkpoint

start
:**open(path)**\nread the 64-byte WAL header;<<#BBDEFB>>
if (magic + version accepted?\n(dual-magic { "PARTWAL\0", "PARTWALO" },\nversion ∈ [MIN_SUPPORTED, VERSION])) then (no)
  :**fail-closed** — refuse the file\n(corrupt magic / too-new version);<<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:decode **checkpoint_lsn**, **commit_seq_floor**,\n**rank_regime** from the header;<<#FFE0B2>>
:**load the last checkpoint image**\n(dense CX snapshot ⇒ the base in-memory trie);<<#BBDEFB>>
note right #BBDEFB
  Everything with LSN ≤ checkpoint_lsn is already
  folded into the image (the checkpoint truncated
  the WAL to the committed watermark), so replay
  only needs the durable tail past checkpoint_lsn.
end note

:**scan the durable WAL tail**\nrecords with LSN > checkpoint_lsn,\nstopping at the first torn / un-fsync'd frame\n(CRC mismatch or short read ⇒ end of durable prefix);<<#BBDEFB>>

partition "reconcile_lww  (per-term, max commit-generation)" {
  :**Pass 1** — collect CommitRank records into\nrank[data_lsn] = generation;<<#FFE0B2>>
  :**Pass 2** — stamp each data record\ngeneration_of(lsn) = rank.get(lsn).unwrap_or(lsn),\napplying the RankRegime drop-rule\n(Overlay + unranked ⇒ DROP orphan);<<#FFE0B2>>
  :**sort** all surviving ops by (generation, lsn)\n= CAS / commit-visibility order;<<#FFE0B2>>
}

if (per term, was the last writer's record\nfsync'd before the crash?) then (yes — acknowledged)
  :**restore** the term to its last committed value\n(redo the winning op);<<#C8E6C9>>
else (no — un-acked / orphan)
  :**drop** — the write was never durable,\nno caller ever saw it succeed;<<#FFCDD2>>
endif

:**rebuild the lock-free overlay**\nby applying the (generation, lsn)-ordered winners;<<#C8E6C9>>
:**resume serving**\n(state == committed-visible membership at crash time);<<#C8E6C9>>
stop

legend right
| Color | Phase |
|<#BBDEFB>| durable on-disk read |
|<#FFE0B2>| control / reconcile |
|<#C8E6C9>| in-memory rebuild / serve |
|<#FFCDD2>| never-durable (dropped) |
endlegend
@enduml
